  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Reading guide",
      "items": [
        "Each arrow from takt is a delegation; dashed arrows to pm, architect and product-designer also cover a lend, where a dispatch switch hands them the user's session; the judge node runs as two blind instances, judge-a and judge-b",
        "VFS capabilities per agent come from agent.yaml; planning and interlocutor agents have none, but keep the native edit allow to deliver documents the user asks for"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Harness",
      "items": [
        "Dispatch admits every delegation and lend switch and keeps the execution history",
        "VFS holds claims, staged work, verdict gates and consolidation; only takt claims and consolidates",
        "Every agent records to Memory with memory_record (not drawn)"
      ]
    }
  ]
